        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "Under aerobic conditions, Ni(NO3)2·6H2O (0.0579 g, 0.1993 mmol), Dy(NO3)3·5H2O (0.0445 g, 0.1016 mmol), di-2-pyridyl ketone (0.0359 g, 0.1951 mmol), H2L (0.0480 g, 0.1975 mmol) and trimethylamine (0.1000 g, 0.9883 mmol) in an approximate 2:1:2:2:10 molar ratio were combined in CH3OH (15 mL) and stirred at room temperature for 15 min. The yellow solution was filtered and the filtrate was left to crystallize by slow evaporation in air. Yellow block crystals of 1 suitable for SCXRD were isolated after 3 days, washed three times with n-hexane and dried in air. Carbonate ligands arise from spontaneous fixation of atmospheric CO2. Eight lattice CH3OH molecules were lost upon drying.",
